he same over-strict bound still in the YoY test one layer down; round 4 fixed it and both reviewers re-PASS (hash c0ad071f). **Whether the display should ever surface a >1 ratio mid-season is deferred to the Stats-tab build.** Then ci-data-build (round 4) failed to BUILD `int_team_season__metrics` — "team_sk is ambiguous": the projection's final SELECT joins `season_final sf` to a `matchdays md` CTE that also exposes team_sk, so the unqualified `team_sk` inside `generate_surrogate_key` was ambiguous. **This was MASKED in rounds 1-3** because the upstream cumulative-test failure SKIPPED building the whole downstream (projection + its direct consumer `mart_team_profile` never ran — so CI had never actually built them). **Round-5 fix = qualify the surrogate-key inputs `sf.team_sk`/`sf.season_sk`** (byte-identity preserved — same hash). Verified via `bq --dry_run`: the projection AND the new YoY both validate, and every mart `y.<col>` exists in the YoY output (hash b90f02d3, both reviewers PASS). **Lesson: a failing upstream test hides downstream BUILD errors in a slim CI run — dry-run the never-built downstream against BQ rather than discovering errors one CI round at a time.** This is the DATA behind the redesigned team Stats tab's per-metric vs-last-season column.
